<title>FRANCE: HORSE RACING-PRIX SAINT-ALARY RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-PRIX SAINT-ALARY RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the Prix Saint-Alary, a</p>
<p>group one race for three-year-old fillies, run over two</p>
<p>kilometres at Longchamp on Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Brilliance (ridden by Olivier Peslier)</p>
<p>2. Fleeting Glimpse (Thierry Jarnet)</p>
<p>3. Gazelle Royale (Thierry Thulliez)</p>
<p>Seven ran.</p>
<p>Distances: Four lengths, short head.</p>
<p>Winner owned by the Ecurie Skymarc Farm and trained in</p>
<p>France by Pascal Bary.</p>
<p>Value to the winner: 94,295 dollars.</p>
<p>Pari-Mutuel (to a one-franc stake): Win 4.50; places 2.40</p>
<p>2.90. Straight Forecast 17.10.</p>
</text>
